From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Palmer <dodava@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:00:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: chipidea: Don't bounce URBs with their own DMA mapping

Since commit 7ab8716713c9 ("usb: chipidea: Fix DMA overwrite for Tegra"),
Tegra uses a bounce buffer for every transfer whose length isn't a
multiple of 4. ci_hdrc_alloc_dma_aligned_buffer() swaps the bounce buffer
into transfer_buffer even when the caller has set URB_NO_TRANSFER_DMA_MAP
and supplied transfer_dma. usb_hcd_map_urb_for_dma() then doesn't map
the bounce buffer, so the controller transfers to and from transfer_dma
as usual. For IN transfers, ci_hdrc_free_dma_aligned_buffer() then copies
the untouched bounce buffer over the data the device sent.

usb-storage does this with its coherent I/O buffer, so on Tegra the
13-byte CSW of every command is corrupted, and the 1-byte Get Max LUN
reply comes back as garbage. USB flash drives get reset over and over
and never appear as disks.

Leave URBs with URB_NO_TRANSFER_DMA_MAP alone.

Fixes: 7ab8716713c9 ("usb: chipidea: Fix DMA overwrite for Tegra")
---
 drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c b/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c
--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c
@@ -417,6 +417,12 @@
 	struct ci_hdrc_dma_aligned_buffer *temp;
 
 	if (urb->num_sgs || urb->sg || urb->transfer_buffer_length == 0)
+		return 0;
+	/*
+	 * The caller has mapped the buffer itself, and the controller uses
+	 * transfer_dma, not a bounce buffer swapped into transfer_buffer.
+	 */
+	if (urb->transfer_flags & URB_NO_TRANSFER_DMA_MAP)
 		return 0;
 	if (IS_ALIGNED((uintptr_t)urb->transfer_buffer, 4)
 	    && IS_ALIGNED(urb->transfer_buffer_length, 4))
